Welcome to the assylum, Ryan.

Stupid risks ... RNG issues ... well, you're no Robinson Crusoe.  If
you don't have any scruples about being spoiled, you will find lots of
advice here to get you further into the dungeon.  After which your
problems will change to overconfidence and overelaboration (trying to
do too much).

I started playing NetHack on my Amiga 500 a little over 15 years ago.
It was v3.3.1 IIRC, and someone will confirm or deny that when I say
that it was a version before the invention of the Mines or Sokoban or
the Quest, and when Rodney held the Amulet.  I ascended in that
non-networked version twice, once as a Barbarian and once as a Samurai.

I highly recommend playing on telnet://nethack.alt.org ... visit the
website at http://alt.org/nethack/ for further information.  If nothing
else, this will give you a chance to pick up bones piles from players
more diverse than yourself, but it also means you will be playing the
most recent version.

